  "notes": "USAGE:\nOriginally a nature term for birds nesting ({巣|す} = nest + {籠|こ}もる = to stay inside), this word became a buzzword during the COVID-19 pandemic. {巣|す}ごもり{消費|しょうひ} and {巣|す}ごもり{需要|じゅよう} became common in business and media to describe the shift in consumer behavior toward home-based activities and purchases.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {巣|す}ごもり{需要|じゅよう}: stay-at-home demand\n- {巣|す}ごもり{消費|しょうひ}: stay-at-home spending\n- {巣|す}ごもり{生活|せいかつ}: stay-at-home lifestyle\n- {巣|す}ごもり{期間|きかん}: period of staying home",
